AMB-1 1.3.2 – studio twin (firmware code for the host), built from https://github.com/charlesvestal/fm1-amb tag v1.3.2
(commit 7c538516d6c52216ff4c8a4881cf2f0dcb07c44b; source: https://github.com/charlesvestal/fm1-amb/archive/7c538516d6c52216ff4c8a4881cf2f0dcb07c44b.tar.gz), with the submodules its tag pins:
  base/: https://github.com/charlesvestal/fm1-base commit 3ae2a65ddd02e15bf9ce925b5a7136d5d207ee25
  base/bsp/: https://github.com/hugelton/felucca-bsp commit f878800967e66e721dfbc9a4f5fe1835772ae8fc
MPL-2.0 (AMB-1 by Charles Vestal; fm1-base, Copyright (C) 2026 Charles Vestal; felucca-bsp, from Felucca, Copyright (C) 2026 Leo Kuroshita (@kurogedelic), Hügelton Instruments).
The Source Code Form of every file is at the commits above; the texts of the licences and of the parts compiled in (the type faces Barlow and Terminus are rasterised in: OFL 1.1) are LICENSE,
LICENSING.md, LICENSING-fm1-base.md, LICENSING-felucca-bsp.md and THIRD_PARTY.txt beside this file. The JieLi SDK files of AMB-1's packages are not part of the twin.
The firmware sources are unmodified. The glue tools/studio/fm1base_studio.c (MPL-2.0, in FM-1 Companion's source) includes them as fm1-base's own
browser emulator does (web/emu/emu_web.c, host/plat_host.c) and adds the device's storage.c on the flash image, the USB SysEx path (the screen reader, felucca-bsp's ota.c
identity handshake) and USB MIDI out; the hardware stand-ins are the emulator's: keys/LEDs/LCD, the MASTER pot, NOR flash = a 1 MiB RAM image, one core,
USB = always configured, no USB audio, no TRS MIDI, no updater and no USB boot, the default panel map (no hardware calibration). Compiled with WASI SDK clang.

Corresponding Source (GNU GPL 3.0, section 6)
The complete corresponding source of this build is https://github.com/charlesvestal/fm1-amb at commit 7c538516d6c52216ff4c8a4881cf2f0dcb07c44b
together with FM-1 Companion's build script tools/build_sims.py, its submodules above and the glue tools/studio/fm1base_studio.c. A tarball of exactly this commit
